cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "WildfireIQ Kamloops"
message: "If you use this software or its derived datasets, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Dang"
    given-names: "Deeparsh Singh"
    affiliation: "Thompson Rivers University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DeeparshSingh/WildfireIQ"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-08"
abstract: >-
  An open platform for wildfire risk, air quality, climate trends and
  community preparedness in British Columbia, built entirely from free
  public data. It includes a pooled multi-region LightGBM wildfire-risk
  classifier scored on 523 H3 hexagons across four regions, a 21-model
  LightGBM quantile forecaster for 48-hour PM2.5 in Kamloops, a Van Wagner
  Fire Weather Index implementation over 27 years of ERA5 reanalysis, a 3D
  CesiumJS globe with six live data layers, a private FireSmart preparedness
  hub, a climate-trend page with Theil-Sen statistics, and a tool-using
  assistant (GLM 5.3 Flash via OpenRouter) that answers only from the
  platform's own data. Built with a Thompson Rivers University Sustainability
  Research Grant, 2025-2026.
keywords:
  - wildfire
  - air-quality
  - climate
  - british-columbia
  - kamloops
  - lightgbm
  - fire-weather-index
  - cesiumjs
  - fastapi
  - llm-agent
